From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: REMOVE=ALL also removes an installed feature whose level is 0

Anki (winget Anki.Anki, an MSI) would not uninstall through SG Store: "Anki
was not removed". msiexec /X ended with success and took the files away,
but the product stayed registered, and RegisterProduct rewrote its
Uninstall entry and InstallProperties. Its DesktopShortcutFeature has level
0, raised to 1 by a Condition row only while the installer's property is
set. It was installed, and at removal it had level 0 again, so
process_state_property skipped it as it skips every level-0 feature. It
stayed installed, check_unpublish saw a feature that was not absent, and
the product was never unpublished.

Windows removes every installed feature on REMOVE=ALL (or when the feature
is named), whatever its level now. A level-0 feature that is installed now
gets the remove request too; features that are not installed are skipped as
before.

Gate test-msilevel0 (64- and 32-bit); mutant SG_MUTANT_MSI_LEVEL0_KEPT.
---
--- a/dlls/msi/action.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/action.c
@@ -1541,7 +1541,16 @@
 
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( feature, &package->features, MSIFEATURE, entry )
     {
+        /* Stained Glass OS: a feature whose level is 0 now is still removed when
+         * it is installed -- Anki's desktop shortcut, level 1 only while its
+         * installer's property was set; REMOVE=ALL left it, and the product
+         * stayed registered with its files gone */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MSI_LEVEL0_KEPT
+        if (feature->Level <= 0 && !(remove && feature->Installed != INSTALLSTATE_ABSENT &&
+                                     feature->Installed != INSTALLSTATE_UNKNOWN))
+#else
         if (feature->Level <= 0)
+#endif
             continue;
 
         if (reinstall)
